      <memberdef kind="function" id="classllvm_1_1_a_arch64_disassembler_1af0d4e965266abd2266d855c2a0a8f278" prot="public" static="no" const="yes" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="virtual">
        <type><ref refid="classuint64__t" kindref="compound">uint64_t</ref></type>
        <definition>uint64_t AArch64Disassembler::suggestBytesToSkip</definition>
        <argsstring>(ArrayRef&lt; uint8_t &gt; Bytes, uint64_t Address) const override</argsstring>
        <name>suggestBytesToSkip</name>
        <qualifiedname>llvm::AArch64Disassembler::suggestBytesToSkip</qualifiedname>
        <reimplements refid="classllvm_1_1_m_c_disassembler_1a7c1ac522bf9b5a8b411e9d78ed69e4b2">suggestBytesToSkip</reimplements>
        <param>
          <type><ref refid="classllvm_1_1_array_ref" kindref="compound">ArrayRef</ref>&lt; <ref refid="classuint8__t" kindref="compound">uint8_t</ref> &gt;</type>
          <declname>Bytes</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type><ref refid="classuint64__t" kindref="compound">uint64_t</ref></type>
          <declname>Address</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Suggest a distance to skip in a buffer of data to find the next place to look for the start of an instruction. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>For example, if all instructions have a fixed alignment, this might advance to the next multiple of that alignment.</para>
<para>If not overridden, the default is 1.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Address</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>- The address, in the memory space of region, of the starting point (typically the first byte of something that did not decode as a valid instruction at all). </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Bytes</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>- A reference to the actual bytes at Address. May be needed in order to determine the width of an unrecognized instruction (e.g. in Thumb this is a simple consistent criterion that doesn&apos;t require knowing the specific instruction). The caller can pass as much data as they have available, and the function is required to make a reasonable default choice if not enough data is available to make a better one. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>- A number of bytes to skip. Must always be greater than zero. May be greater than the size of Bytes. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
